  "case_version": 1,
  "name": "joint-infeasibility-two-scenarios",
  "description": "A single egress switch at px-b must separate two requests that share identity, service and label. Only timing can separate them, because req-old is only eligible for svc-old and req-new only for svc-new, and each version of the switch serves exactly one of those services on px-b; both versions keep each request's own label, so the service that finally receives a request decides eligibility. In the baseline scenario req-old leaves px-b at step 0 and req-new arrives at step 3, so the switch slot must be in {1, 2}. In inverted-reach the two entry delays are swapped, so the switch would have to be both after step 3 and before step 0. Each scenario therefore has a legal table of its own (baseline at 1 or 2, inverted at 2), but the intersection is empty. plan reports E_UNSATISFIABLE. The baseline order has no pairwise scheduling conflict, so the report gives the shortest reachability failure prefix instead.",
